00:01:04.186 --> 00:01:06.120
and now lives in a trailer instead,

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.671
so naturally I wanted to meet her;

00:01:07.671 --> 00:01:10.799
spend 24 hours in her shoes
doing anything and everything

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:12.591
that she would naturally.

00:01:12.591 --> 00:01:14.022
- [Woman] Alright, you read to do this?

00:01:14.022 --> 00:01:15.151
- I'm ready.

00:01:15.151 --> 00:01:15.984
Let's go.

00:01:16.937 --> 00:01:20.440
Just gonna call Beth who
is Lynea's assistant.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.549
- [Beth] Hello, this is Beth.

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:23.578
- [Tania] Hi Beth, it's
Tan from Buzzfeed here.

00:01:23.578 --> 00:01:25.315
We've just pulled into your car park.

00:01:25.315 --> 00:01:27.483
- [Beth] Okay, I will
come get you right now.

00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:29.472
- I've already seen five cats.

00:01:29.472 --> 00:01:30.722
Only 995 to go.

00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:34.908
I'm about to meet the ultimate cat lady.

00:01:34.908 --> 00:01:37.746
Do you know how that feels?

00:01:37.746 --> 00:01:38.579
- [Woman] I don't know.

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:39.412
How do you feel?

00:01:39.412 --> 00:01:41.265
- [Tania] It's a privilege, it's an honor,

00:01:41.265 --> 00:01:44.015
and it's a little bit terrifying.

00:01:45.207 --> 00:01:46.651
- We do lock up at four o'clock,

00:01:46.651 --> 00:01:49.096
so these gates lock, but she'll
probably give you the code

00:01:49.096 --> 00:01:51.483
so in case you want to go out
and get dinner or anything.

00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:52.316
- [Tania] Hey guys.

00:01:52.316 --> 00:01:53.214
- [Beth] Chip, Toto.

00:01:53.214 --> 00:01:54.047
- Hello.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.268
Nice to officially meet you.

00:01:55.268 --> 00:01:56.128
- Yes, and you're from Australia?

00:01:56.128 --> 00:01:57.020
- I am.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.539
I'm from Australia.
(cat meows)

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:00.372
- Daphne!

00:02:00.372 --> 00:02:01.705
Sophia, Sophia.

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:02.704
- [Tania Voiceover] When I first got there

00:02:02.704 --> 00:02:06.092
I was instantly gobsmacked
at how big her property was.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.943
She had peacocks for fuck's sake.

00:02:07.943 --> 00:02:10.447
I could feel a little bit of
apprehension from her at first,

00:02:10.447 --> 00:02:11.508
and you know, I get it.

00:02:11.508 --> 00:02:12.779
It's easy to take the piece.

00:02:12.779 --> 00:02:15.358
Cat ladies are the butt
of so many generic gags,

00:02:15.358 --> 00:02:17.419
but it wasn't long she started telling me

00:02:17.419 --> 00:02:20.145
a little more about what it
takes to be obsessed with cats.

00:02:20.145 --> 00:02:22.430
And then she took me on a
little tour of the grounds.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:25.443
- I moved out of my 4,200 square foot,

00:02:25.443 --> 00:02:28.808
five bedroom home, and gave it to the cats

00:02:28.808 --> 00:02:29.893
and I live in a trailer.

00:02:29.893 --> 00:02:32.664
I was normal for many years of my life,

00:02:32.664 --> 00:02:35.706
and then I got a divorce, and then I went

00:02:35.706 --> 00:02:38.838
through some traumatic situations.

00:02:38.838 --> 00:02:40.286
I kept saying to myself you're supposed

00:02:40.286 --> 00:02:41.933
to be doing something with your life.

00:02:41.933 --> 00:02:43.422
I never really knew what it was.

00:02:43.422 --> 00:02:45.668
Then after I started rescue, I realized

00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:48.186
that you bought a 4,200 square foot,

00:02:48.186 --> 00:02:51.290
five bedroom home on six acres

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.022
and you're single with no kids.

00:02:53.022 --> 00:02:57.189
Then this started and I go,
somebody planned this for me.

00:02:58.357 --> 00:03:00.896
So I worked for three years at a vet.

00:03:00.896 --> 00:03:01.729
- [Tania] And how did you know

00:03:01.729 --> 00:03:04.975
when it was time to give
your house over to the cats?

00:03:04.975 --> 00:03:06.319
- They would jump from the top

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:09.078
onto my solar plexus in
the middle of the night

00:03:09.078 --> 00:03:11.512
and then they would run
across my face fighting,

00:03:11.512 --> 00:03:15.306
and I have scars, and then
they threw up in my ear.

00:03:15.306 --> 00:03:16.581
- [Tania] Excellent.

00:03:16.581 --> 00:03:17.780
- [Tania Voiceover] I
was a little bit confused

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.854
about some parts of the conversation.

00:03:19.854 --> 00:03:21.304
- Oh, there's that,
the black and white one

00:03:21.304 --> 00:03:22.775
is the one that was exiled.

00:03:22.775 --> 00:03:26.376
His name is Sultan but
I changed it to Isis.

00:03:26.376 --> 00:03:28.394
His name is Afghanistan.

00:03:28.394 --> 00:03:30.685
You wonder about Middle Eastern men.

00:03:30.685 --> 00:03:32.079
- [Tania Voiceover] She
knows I'm Arab, right?

00:03:32.079 --> 00:03:33.971
But otherwise, most of it was cool.

00:03:33.971 --> 00:03:35.553
So she's invested her retirement

00:03:35.553 --> 00:03:38.407
in building separate
ICUs in various sections

00:03:38.407 --> 00:03:39.986
throughout her property for the sick,

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.621
old, young, and in betweens.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.285
- [Lynea] And in the
winter they have heaters

00:03:43.285 --> 00:03:44.878
and in the summer they have misters

00:03:44.878 --> 00:03:47.614
and ceiling fans and a water cooler.

00:03:47.614 --> 00:03:49.968
- [Tania Voiceover] Basically,
they live better than me, ya.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.291
