00:09:20.754 --> 00:09:21.587
- [Tania] So much.

00:09:21.587 --> 00:09:22.681
- You did a great job.

00:09:22.681 --> 00:09:24.840
- [Tania Voiceover] And then
she suggested we get some air.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:26.319
- [Lynea] We could take a walk.

00:09:26.319 --> 00:09:27.220
I take a gun.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.112
Is that alright with you?

00:09:28.112 --> 00:09:29.718
- [Tania Voiceover] Guns
aren't big in Australia.

00:09:29.718 --> 00:09:31.258
- And we're taking your gun with us?

00:09:31.258 --> 00:09:35.425
- When you're out there, there's
nobody but you, hopefully.

00:09:36.287 --> 00:09:39.301
And that if a coyote comes,
I've had 'em challenge us

00:09:39.301 --> 00:09:41.713
and I've had 'em try to
take one of the dogs,

00:09:41.713 --> 00:09:44.567
that anything that makes
noise is a good thing.

00:09:44.567 --> 00:09:47.886
Two rottweilers and a 38-Special
and you know you're safe.

00:09:47.886 --> 00:09:48.719
Okay?

00:09:48.719 --> 00:09:49.678
That's yours.

00:09:49.678 --> 00:09:52.907
I don't normally shoot
unless a coyote attacks,

00:09:52.907 --> 00:09:54.626
but since you wanted to see what it's like

00:09:54.626 --> 00:09:57.891
to live out in the country, we'll go.

00:09:57.891 --> 00:09:59.232
Shoot at that sign.

00:09:59.232 --> 00:10:01.734
(lively Caribbean music)

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:03.812
You can pull the hammer back.

00:10:03.812 --> 00:10:05.379
- [Tania Voiceover] As if
I know how to shoot a gun.

00:10:05.379 --> 00:10:06.279
- What's the hammer?

00:10:06.279 --> 00:10:07.570
It's loaded?

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:08.731
(gun fires)

00:10:08.731 --> 00:10:10.176
(lively Caribbean music)

00:10:10.176 --> 00:10:11.009
- [Lynea] Aim.

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:13.353
- Again?
(gun fires)

00:10:13.353 --> 00:10:14.265
I don't even know where that one went.

00:10:14.265 --> 00:10:15.549
- [Lynea] That one went wild. (laughs)

00:10:15.549 --> 00:10:17.346
- This is such a lovely bonding exercise.

00:10:17.346 --> 00:10:19.235
- [Lynea] Ya, then we'll
let you use the shotgun.

00:10:19.235 --> 00:10:21.583
So grab a couple of those.

00:10:21.583 --> 00:10:22.416
- What?

00:10:23.374 --> 00:10:25.090
(lively Caribbean music)

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.423
(gun fires)

00:10:29.306 --> 00:10:30.550
(gun fires)

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.575
- Next we're gonna go
look for coyote skulls.

00:10:32.575 --> 00:10:33.895
- Alright.

00:10:33.895 --> 00:10:34.778
What a morning.

00:10:34.778 --> 00:10:36.380
I haven't even had breakfast yet.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:37.622
- [Tania Voiceover]
Lynea was talking about

00:10:37.622 --> 00:10:40.231
how she found a dead
coyote a month or so ago

00:10:40.231 --> 00:10:42.031
in a field and wanted the skull.

00:10:42.031 --> 00:10:45.046
So after our bonding sesh
we headed over and found it.

00:10:45.046 --> 00:10:47.844
I mean, this has absolutely
nothing to do with cats,

00:10:47.844 --> 00:10:49.179
and you know, I'm a vegetarian,

00:10:49.179 --> 00:10:51.078
but it was still her time
so why not include it

00:10:51.078 --> 00:10:53.291
in this video, ya?

00:10:53.291 --> 00:10:55.729
- [Lynea] I don't know how
people dismember human beings.

00:10:55.729 --> 00:10:56.628
Here, your turn.

00:10:56.628 --> 00:10:58.379
- [Tania] Wow. (sighs)

00:10:58.379 --> 00:10:59.954
- Okay, you're the bag lady.

00:10:59.954 --> 00:11:02.366
And you're taking this home, right?

00:11:02.366 --> 00:11:03.546
No?

00:11:03.546 --> 00:11:06.544
- So we've been up for six hours,

00:11:06.544 --> 00:11:09.709
shoveled a lot of shit,
fed hundreds of mouths,

00:11:09.709 --> 00:11:12.597
cut off a coyote's head, shot some guns.

00:11:12.597 --> 00:11:13.944
Probably should just have a glass of water

00:11:13.944 --> 00:11:16.859
and a nap right about now.
(goose honks)

00:11:16.859 --> 00:11:17.919
- [Tania Voiceover] And then suddenly

00:11:17.919 --> 00:11:19.152
we were having our last words.

00:11:19.152 --> 00:11:23.268
- My obsession with cats
I've kept in control.

00:11:23.268 --> 00:11:26.838
I have never taken in more
cats than I can afford.

00:11:26.838 --> 00:11:29.638
So I feel that because
I can take care of them

00:11:29.638 --> 00:11:31.228
and I spay and neuter 'em all,

00:11:31.228 --> 00:11:34.754
and that the facility is
good and the cats are healthy

00:11:34.754 --> 00:11:37.389
that it's not a bad obsession.

00:11:37.389 --> 00:11:41.556
I gave up my retirement, my
home, and my life for cats.

00:11:42.581 --> 00:11:43.823
- [Tania] Would you have it any other way?

00:11:43.823 --> 00:11:45.370
- I have no regrets.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.016
The people that don't
agree with what I do,

00:11:48.016 --> 00:11:49.918
they think I've gone overboard.

00:11:49.918 --> 00:11:52.011
They think that there's
something wrong with me.

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:53.543
- [Tania] What do you think?

00:11:53.543 --> 00:11:55.368
- I think maybe they're right.

00:11:55.368 --> 00:11:59.232
I am obsessed about it, but
my obsession is to the point

00:11:59.232 --> 00:12:02.828
where this is the most
important part of my life,

00:12:02.828 --> 00:12:04.143
and I don't mind.

00:12:04.143 --> 00:12:05.230
- [Tania Voiceover] I
mean, at the end of the day

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:06.948
this obsession had done a lot of good.

00:12:06.948 --> 00:12:10.351
- We have rescued 30,000 plus cats

00:12:10.351 --> 00:12:12.833
and 8,000 plus dogs.

00:12:12.833 --> 00:12:15.120
The county hasn't taken
in cats, even to kill 'em

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.611
for over five years.

00:12:16.611 --> 00:12:19.018
There's 200,000 on the streets.

00:12:19.018 --> 00:12:20.685
So, we get them out.

00:12:21.768 --> 00:12:24.067
We're like the Costco, the wholesaler.

00:12:24.067 --> 00:12:25.236
They were newborns when they came

00:12:25.236 --> 00:12:27.215
and they were all covered in metal.

00:12:27.215 --> 00:12:30.215
I want to fix it and I can't fix it,

00:12:31.204 --> 00:12:34.677
and I get angry and I
just, puts me into the

00:12:34.677 --> 00:12:36.346
well, I've gotta save more.

00:12:36.346 --> 00:12:37.437
- [Tania Voiceover] And I kinda get it.

00:12:37.437 --> 00:12:38.726
It's so easy to look at someone

00:12:38.726 --> 00:12:41.114
and call their lifestyle unhealthy,

00:12:41.114 --> 00:12:42.946
but she's got something
that gives her meaning.

00:12:42.946 --> 00:12:45.009
- To me it is just a way of life.

00:12:45.009 --> 00:12:47.257
I get up in the morning and I'm happy.

00:12:47.257 --> 00:12:48.707
That's all that counts.

00:12:48.707 --> 00:12:49.898
- [Tania] I guess the majority of the time

00:12:49.898 --> 00:12:52.743
we see obsessions as negative things,

00:12:52.743 --> 00:12:55.832
things that can overwhelm
us and restrict us,

00:12:55.832 --> 00:12:58.127
but Lynea sees her obsession as something

00:12:58.127 --> 00:13:00.585
that's really positive
and it gives her life

00:13:00.585 --> 00:13:03.013
a lot of meaning which is really cool.

00:13:03.013 --> 00:13:05.486
For her, it's just life, it's normal

00:13:05.486 --> 00:13:07.268
as it is for us to be obsessed

00:13:07.268 --> 00:13:09.591
with the things that we love in life.

